      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Penta Application Screener</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-500">An internal review tool for the Penta Housing Co-op membership committee</p>
    </header>

    <div class="rounded-xl bg-white p-8 shadow-lg space-y-8 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">What it is</h2>
        <p>The <strong>Penta Application Screener</strong> is a private, internal web application used by the membership committee of Penta Housing Co-Operative Association to review applications for membership in the co-op. It is not a public service; access is limited to authorized committee members, who sign in at <a class="text-green-700 underline hover:text-green-800" href="https://screener.pentacoop.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">screener.pentacoop.com</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">What it does</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">When people apply to join the co-op, their responses are collected in a Google Sheet. The screener helps the committee work through those applications by:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 mb-3">
          <li>reading the submitted applications from the co-op's Google Sheet;</li>
          <li>applying the co-op's eligibility rules (such as household size and income ranges);</li>
          <li>helping committee members organize, compare, and prioritize applications into a shortlist for the committee to consider.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The tool supports the committee's work; it does not make membership decisions. Final decisions are always made by people, following the co-op's bylaws and process.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">How it uses Google sign-in</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">Committee members sign in with their Google account for identity only. Signing in does not give the app access to a member's Google Drive, Gmail, or other Google data. Separately, an authorized administrator connects the single Google Sheet of application responses using Google's file picker, which grants read-only access to that one file so the committee can review submissions.</p>
        <p>For full detail on what information the app collects and how it is used, see our <a class="text-green-700 underline hover:text-green-800" href="/privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
      </section>
